# What the image build does NOT need.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and then builds ./cmd/loonsite, so everything
# not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon as build context on every build.
# That was ~35 MB of material the compiler never looks at — reference
# screenshots and example sites — which is time on every `docker compose up
# --build` and a larger cache layer to invalidate.
#
# web/ is NOT excluded and must not be: templates and static assets are
# embedded into the binary from there.

.git
.github

# Reference screenshots for the dev UI inspector, and the example indexer
# sites read while writing docs/BENCHMARK.md. Neither is built or shipped.
refs/
examples/
docs/

# Local tooling: the checks run outside the image.
scripts/
Makefile
.golangci.yml
.editorconfig

# Compose files and their overlays configure the image; they are not in it.
docker-compose.yml
compose.*.yml
deploy/

# Prose.
*.md
LICENSE

# Build and test leftovers.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.test
*.out
coverage.out

# A developer's workspace file points at sibling checkouts that do not exist in
# the container. GOWORK=off already protects the build; this keeps it out of
# the context entirely.
go.work
go.work.sum
